DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       cclleeaarr  clears your terminal's screen if this is possible, including the
       terminal's scrollback buffer (if the extended “E3”  capability  is  de‐
       fined).   cclleeaarr looks in the environment for the terminal type given by
       the environment variable TTEERRMM, and then in the tteerrmmiinnffoo database to de‐
       termine how to clear the screen.

       cclleeaarr  writes  to  the  standard output.  You can redirect the standard
       output to a file (which  prevents  cclleeaarr  from  actually  clearing  the
       screen),  and  later  ccaatt  the  file to the screen, clearing it at that
       point.

